<title>CANADA: Inmet Q3 turns to loss after writedown.</title>
<headline>Inmet Q3 turns to loss after writedown.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr	   loss	C$4.46   profit	C$0.22</p>
<p> Net	   loss     361,765   profit	18,839</p>
<p> Revs		     175,911		  285,870</p>
<p>	   9  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr	   loss	C$4.57     loss	C$2.39</p>
<p> Net	   loss     368,177     loss     191,022</p>
<p> Revs		     737,054		  867,371</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  81,207		   81,207</p>
<p>(All data above 0000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>Note: Full name is Inmet Mining Corp. Results include a C$355 million writedown in the third quarter following a review of the viability of the company's operations and properties. The writedown includes C$69 million from cessation of mining at Copper Range, C$25 million from the shutdown of Bougrine, C$155 million from its investment in Cayeli and C$76 million from Izok Lake.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100</p>
